.nh
.TH "SOROLENS" "1" "Nov 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
sorolens-events-tail - Stream a contract's events live as they are indexed


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsorolens events tail --contract  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Tail a contract's events using the Sorolens server-sent events endpoint.

.PP
Unlike "sorolens events ", which returns a page of already-indexed
events, tail keeps the connection open and pretty-prints each event as it
arrives. Press Ctrl-C to close the stream.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--contract\fP=""
	Contract ID to stream events for (required)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tail


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API key for authenticating with the Sorolens API

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Sorolens API base URL

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--network\fP=""
	Stellar network (testnet, mainnet, futurenet, standalone)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--output\fP=""
	Output format (table, json, yaml or jsonl)

.PP
\fB--plugin-api-key\fP[=false]
	When dispatching to a plugin, pass the active profile's API key as SOROLENS_API_KEY (off by default)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Configuration profile name (default: $SOROLENS_PROFILE, then the default profile)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	jq-style path filter applied to structured output (e.g. '.items[].name')

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=10s
	Request timeout


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsorolens-events(1)\fP
